---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/common/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { METADATA_REGISTRY } from '../lib/seo/metadata';

const meta = METADATA_REGISTRY['/privacy-policy'];

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy' },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title={meta.title}
  description={meta.description}
  canonical={meta.canonical}
  robots={meta.robots}
>
  <div class="bg-white border-b border-marketing-border py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-4">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs font-mono text-marketing-muted">Last Updated: August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="py-16 sm:py-20 bg-marketing-bg border-b border-marketing-border">
    <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-8 text-sm text-zinc-700 leading-relaxed prose-measure">
      
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-900">1. Overview & Core Privacy Guarantee</h2>
        <p>
          At FrameProof, privacy is not a marketing setting—it is the foundational engineering principle of our software. FrameProof operates as a browser-first client-side application. When you drop images, contact sheets, or collages into FrameProof, all image decoding, resizing, layout generation, and PDF document exports happen directly within your browser's local memory sandbox.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Your photos, image pixels, original camera filenames, and EXIF metadata are never transmitted to our servers or stored in any remote database.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-900">2. Information We Do Not Collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li>We do not collect or store user accounts, passwords, or login credentials.</li>
          <li>We do not collect, view, or retain uploaded image files or photos.</li>
          <li>We do not inspect or transmit embedded EXIF camera data (GPS, camera serials, timestamps).</li>
          <li>We do not track individual photo selections or client review statuses.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-900">3. Local Storage and Session Manifests</h2>
        <p>
          If you choose to export a project manifest (<code>.frameproof.json</code>), this file is generated client-side and saved directly to your local file system. When re-opened, it is read entirely within your browser to restore layout parameters.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-900">4. Third-Party Services & Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We may use minimal, privacy-respecting website analytics to track coarse aggregated statistics (such as total page visits and browser operating systems). No media files or user identifiers are ever included in telemetry events.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-900">5. Contact Regarding Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          For any questions or verifications regarding FrameProof's local architecture, contact us at <code>privacy@frameproof.com</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
